WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.340
Many ribosomes can read
one mRNA at the same time.

2
00:00:04.390 --> 00:00:07.770
Each builds its own copy
of the same polypeptide,

3
00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:10.190
one amino acid after another.

4
00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:13.250
But the amino acids are
not made from the message.

5
00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:16.130
They already float free in the cytoplasm.

6
00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:19.610
A ribosome never sees
an amino acid's name.

7
00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:25.230
So how does it build the right protein,
with the right amino acid in every place?

8
00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:28.370
In this mission, you'll
take the ribosome apart:

9
00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:31.870
two subunits, made of RNA and protein.

10
00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:35.700
Then you'll decode a short
gene, codon by codon,

11
00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:38.040
into a chain of amino acids.

12
00:00:38.090 --> 00:00:43.360
Your mission: find out how a ribosome
builds the right protein without ever seeing

13
00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:44.830
an amino acid's name.
